From 54b1a2693ef263b95c9507d23627bea837819d31 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Henrik Klee <henrik@goat-code.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 23:12:31 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Report text input facts to an on-screen keyboard listener

An on-screen keyboard has to open when the person taps a text field,
not whenever a program moves focus or a press becomes a text selection,
and to step aside while someone types on a physical keyboard. Only the
compositor sees the facts that decide this; the decision itself is
policy, so it belongs to one program the desktop provides rather than
to the compositor.

Add <onScreenKeyboard listener="command" />. Labwc starts the listener
once and writes one line per fact to its standard input: a focused
text field going on (with the client's text-input version) or off, the
client asking for an input panel to be shown or hidden, a press on the
keyboard-focused surface and its release (how long it lasted and how
far it moved), a key of the typing block pressed on a physical
keyboard, and how many physical keyboards with letter keys there are.
The pipe does not block; a listener that stops reading loses lines, the
compositor never waits.

With a listener set, text-inputs get keyboard focus even when no input
method is bound, so that clients report their fields at all.

Assisted-by: LLM
